                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4e4ad3bb-1806-3f9c-8007-23d1c292dd14",
                        "entry_id": "727873f7-a485-3d95-8f9c-34ecdbe5158e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "viola, violet"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "relational"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7b02ce7-a4a1-42a7-8809-6bb8d9c458ff",
                                "sense_id": "4e4ad3bb-1806-3f9c-8007-23d1c292dd14",
                                "text": "Богато, но по годам была одета его жена, женщина крупная, широкая и спокойная; сложно, но легко и прозрачно, с невинной откровенностью — дочь, высокая, тонкая, с великолепными волосами, прелестно убранными, с ароматическим от фиалковых лепёшечек дыханием и с нежнейшими розовыми прыщиками возле губ и между лопаток, чуть припудренных…",
                                "translation": "Rich, yet in keeping with her years, was the attire of his wife,—a big, broad, calm woman; elaborate, yet light and diaphanous, with an innocent frankness, was that of his daughter,—a girl innocently frank, tall, slender, with magnificent hair, exquisitely dressed, with breath aromatic from violet cachous with the tenderest of tiny moles about her lips and between her shoulder blades, slightly powdered. . . .",
                                "english": "Rich, yet in keeping with her years, was the attire of his wife,—a big, broad, calm woman; elaborate, yet light and diaphanous, with an innocent frankness, was that of his daughter,—a girl innocently frank, tall, slender, with magnificent hair, exquisitely dressed, with breath aromatic from violet cachous with the tenderest of tiny moles about her lips and between her shoulder blades, slightly powdered. . . ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "ec40a6cb-be87-31c8-a513-c6e131d7ba25",
                "word": "фиалковый",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a4e32ea4-5e90-38c3-b907-a8b5bf71230f",
                        "entry_id": "ec40a6cb-be87-31c8-a513-c6e131d7ba25",
                        "glosses": [
                            "изготовленный из фиалки или фиалок"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1f8a85ad-27fb-31d3-a445-fdfa0dd55d90",
                        "entry_id": "ec40a6cb-be87-31c8-a513-c6e131d7ba25",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свойственный фиалкам, напоминающий цветом, формой или запахом фиалку"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca6355a3-c65b-4a17-baec-657fe57d34f4",
                                "sense_id": "1f8a85ad-27fb-31d3-a445-fdfa0dd55d90",
                                "text": "У меня всё по-домашнему, — нежно сказала она, подняв на меня глаза (то ли агатовые, то ли фиалковые, уже не помню, но точно прекрасные) — я сделаю ужин, как мама нас с братом кормила, когда мы были маленькие…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "03b3537d-d8c5-4aab-b7e6-0200be275061",
                        "source_entry_id": "ec40a6cb-be87-31c8-a513-c6e131d7ba25",
                        "target_lang_word": "violaceous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "violaceous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4149883f-9649-34aa-8301-1abb7057f104",
                                        "entry_id": "45668c45-f8c4-3cdb-bb4e-43ac0902dfab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Violet-colored."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af0949df-9560-4ee7-bbcd-00db077b5a5c",
                                                "sense_id": "4149883f-9649-34aa-8301-1abb7057f104",
                                                "text": "These were power heels, and they were worn by women from all over the world. […] They were amaranthine and violaceous and subtly velvet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce290e22-6203-49c1-af98-a9100829a37e",
                        "source_entry_id": "ec40a6cb-be87-31c8-a513-c6e131d7ba25",
                        "target_lang_word": "violet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "violet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc56d64f-7cc8-3708-8c63-e36167ee74c9",
                                        "entry_id": "cd0cb5e3-4825-3765-abc4-72040e0fbc76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata; (inexact) similar-looking plants and flowers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fec76d2b-412e-4929-bdc2-881a560f840c",
                                                "sense_id": "cc56d64f-7cc8-3708-8c63-e36167ee74c9",
                                                "text": "Refreshed by their cooling bath of evening dew, the violets and other nocturnal flowers emitted a pleasant fragrance over the fields, but from the bogs and the rivulets came up now and then damp, penetrating gusts, that sent an icy chill through me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5384052c-0395-4883-85d8-b9eb492f1e9d",
                                                "sense_id": "cc56d64f-7cc8-3708-8c63-e36167ee74c9",
                                                "text": "Albertus Magnus, the thirteenth century philosopher and occultist, states that coriander, valerian, and violet are love producing herbs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4a44ffc-88b8-3658-a3a9-06c08b4bc2d0",
                                        "entry_id": "cd0cb5e3-4825-3765-abc4-72040e0fbc76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90af45ce-54cb-4af0-82bf-1f050ea2aad5",
                                                "sense_id": "f4a44ffc-88b8-3658-a3a9-06c08b4bc2d0",
                                                "text": "‘Tom,’ he said, ‘you are looking at a crushed violet, a spent egg, a squeezed tube.’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0310b327-3799-35f8-9761-dd7537bfd98e",
                                        "entry_id": "cd0cb5e3-4825-3765-abc4-72040e0fbc76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The color of most violets; the colour evoked by the shortest visible wavelengths between 380 and 435 nm, an additive tertiary colour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
